# Derived from mask/src/executor.rs add_flag_variables: mask always sets optional
# args (to "" when absent), so a value from the caller's environment never leaks in.
input: arguments_and_flags__does_not_fail_when_optional_arg_is_not_present.md
env: optional=LEAKED
args: with_opt "I am required"
stdout-not-contains: LEAKED
xfail: kevin leaves an absent optional argument unset, so a same-named variable from the parent environment (or from a calling task via $KEVIN) leaks into the script
